  "id": "COMPOUND:17935 - PROTEIN:1146",
  "verbalization": "Protobioside is implicated in the targeting of multiple entities, ultimately leading to the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit. The evidence suggests that Protobioside acts as a target for SK-HEP1, which in turn is targeted by Suksdorfin. Suksdorfin is known to interact with Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit, establishing a direct pathway from Protobioside to this target. Additionally, Protobioside is also shown to target Endothelial lipase, which is subsequently targeted by two different compounds, both of which are themselves targeted by Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit. This indicates a broader network of interactions where Protobioside may influence the activity of these compounds, potentially modulating the function of Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Protobioside could exert its effects, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
